===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|square||ed-form}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|geometry}} Covered with a [[grid]] of [[square]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The children were taught to plot graphs on '''squared''' paper.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} [[raise|Raised]] to the [[second]] [[power]].
# {{lb|en|chess|in combination}} Located on the specified kind of square on the board.
#: {{ux|en|a light-'''squared''' bishop}}

====Usage notes====
When used attributively in the mathematical sense and applied to a phrase representing a mathematical or physical quantity, the adjective is usually postpositive, as in “3 squared plus 4 squared equals 5 squared”.

